invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: the AES-GCM suite build on AES=extern stops needing
  CH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME, so the image's ch_aes_block gets every
  TLS traffic key, AES-128 and AES-256, and nobody states that the
  peripheral behind it runs in constant time. No mechanism in this tree
  can observe a peripheral's timing, so the firmware author's statement
  is the whole of the claim, and this edit drops the line that asks for
  it (docs/decisions.md 68). quic-builds.sh compiles ct.h under the suite
  on AES=extern without the statement and requires the refusal.

--- old
#ifndef CH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME
#error "CH_SUITE_AES_GCM on AES=extern needs -DCH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME (aes_block.h)"
#endif
--- new
